From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: aurora: disable unsupported shared QCE

Linux 7.3-rc5 marks CRYPTO_DEV_QCE as BROKEN: the driver cannot arbitrate
access with secure world and can race its requests. Aurora therefore has
no QCE driver, but the SoC node defaults to enabled and holds interconnect
sync_state pending forever. Disable this Linux consumer on the board;
leave the remote-controlled BAM and secure-world ownership untouched.
CPU crypto remains available. Do not override BROKEN to quiet the warning.

Reference: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v7.3-rc5/drivers/crypto/Kconfig
Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-xiaomi-aurora.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-xiaomi-aurora.dts
@@ -15,6 +15,10 @@
 #include "pm8550vs.dtsi"
 #include "pmk8550.dtsi"
 
+&crypto {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 &gpu {
 	status = "okay";
 };
